[phase] Contract
[delegate] architect <- Author the Rust migration contract in analysis/brief.md for the NandC project. Use analysis/source-map.md and meta/plan.md as the source of truth. The contract must: (1) define the target crate layout (e.g. src/lib.rs for the gate/arithmetic API, src/main.rs or a tests/ harness for the exhaustive 4-bit add/sub checks); (2) map every public C symbol to its Rust equivalent — nand, not, or, and, xor, add_bit, half_sub, sub_bit, bll, print_add_bit, add_u4, sub_u4, the u4 type alias, and the U4_MAX constant — specifying exact Rust signatures, visibility (pub vs private), and return conventions (replace C bool* out-params with &mut or tuple returns; replace const char* with &str; replace printf/fprintf with println!/eprintln!); (3) state the C→Rust construct mappings (typedef→type, #define→const, static linkage→visibility, C for-loops→for x in range, ternary→if/else); (4) define the test strategy (exhaustive 4-bit add/sub against native Rust arithmetic, mirroring test.c's check_add/check_sub); and (5) specify the build/test toolchain (cargo build, cargo test) and any coverage approach. Keep the contract self-contained so a translator can implement it without re-reading the C source.
[delegate] validator <- Validate the Rust migration contract at analysis/brief.md against the source map (analysis/source-map.md) and meta/plan.md. Confirm: (1) every public C symbol (nand, not, or, and, xor, add_bit, half_sub, sub_bit, bll, print_add_bit, add_u4, sub_u4, u4, U4_MAX) has an exact Rust signature, visibility, and return convention; (2) all C→Rust construct mappings are stated (typedef→type, #define→const, static→visibility, for-loops→range, ternary→if/else, bool* out-params→&mut/tuple, const char*→&str, printf→println!/eprintln!); (3) the target crate layout (src/lib.rs, tests/nand.rs, Cargo.toml) is fully specified; (4) the test strategy (exhaustive 4-bit add/sub mirroring check_add/check_sub) is defined; (5) the build/test toolchain (cargo build, cargo test, coverage) is stated; and (6) the contract is self-contained so a translator can implement it without re-reading the C source. Report any gaps, inconsistencies, or missing symbols as a pass/fail verdict with specifics.
